{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And afterward she bore a daughter.</b> No pregnancy is written of her, to teach you that she was a twin to Zevulun. Another interpretation: no pregnancy is written of her because she was a daughter only at the moment of birth, but throughout the pregnancy she was a male, and Leah judged this herself, as Rashi explained. And Yosef was exchanged for Dinah, as the liturgical poet established: 'a fetus to be exchanged in the womb for a sister.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:43.609975646Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}